# AI Scholar Hub — Maintainer README

LibreChat + MongoDB + Meilisearch + pgvector/rag_api + Gemini, self-hosted
on an Ubuntu VM (Azure) behind Apache. Also runs a separate Admin Panel
service. This file is the fast-reference; full detail lives in
`INSTRUCTIONS.md`, `docs/RUNBOOK.md`, `docs/SCALING.md`, `deploy/README.md`.

## Architecture, in one line each

| Service | Role | Container name |
|---|---|---|
| `api` | LibreChat itself | `AI_Scholar_Hub` |
| `mongodb` | users, chats, balances | `chat-mongodb` |
| `meilisearch` | conversation search (NOT RAG) | `chat-meilisearch` |
| `vectordb` | pgvector store for RAG | `vectordb` |
| `rag_api` | chunks/embeds uploaded docs | `rag_api` |
| `admin-panel` | config/role GUI | `aischolarhub-admin-panel` |

Public URLs: `aischolarhub.seedsnet.org` (main), `admin-ai.seedsnet.org` (admin panel).
All backend ports are `127.0.0.1`-only — Apache is the only public entry point.

## Daily commands

```bash
cd /opt/aischolarhub

docker compose ps -a              # status of everything
docker compose logs -f api        # tail one service
docker compose up -d              # apply compose/env changes (recreates changed containers)
docker compose restart api        # restart without config changes
docker compose down               # stop everything — does NOT touch bind-mounted data
```

## User management — all run via `docker exec`, NOT `npm run`

**`npm run create-user` etc. are broken** on this image (confirmed upstream
bug, [danny-avila/LibreChat#12616](https://github.com/danny-avila/LibreChat/issues/12616)) —
always call the script directly:

```bash
# Create a user — email, name, username, password, in that order
docker exec AI_Scholar_Hub node /app/config/create-user.js \
  student@seedsnet.org "Student Name" studentname TempPass123! --email-verified=True

# Promote to admin (create-user has no reliable --admin flag; do it directly)
docker exec -it chat-mongodb mongosh LibreChat --eval \
  'db.users.updateOne({email: "student@seedsnet.org"}, {$set: {role: "ADMIN"}})'

# Set/adjust token balance
docker exec AI_Scholar_Hub node /app/config/set-balance.js student@seedsnet.org 200000

# List all balances
docker exec -it AI_Scholar_Hub node /app/config/list-balances.js

# Reset a password — INTERACTIVE, needs -it, do not pass args
docker exec -it AI_Scholar_Hub node /app/config/reset-password.js

# Bulk-provision a roster (email,name,temp_password,role,token_quota)
python3 scripts/bulk_import.py students.csv --container AI_Scholar_Hub --domain seedsnet.org --dry-run
python3 scripts/bulk_import.py students.csv --container AI_Scholar_Hub --domain seedsnet.org
```

`--email-verified=True` on `create-user` is **required**, not optional —
without it the script hangs forever on an interactive prompt that
`docker exec` can never answer (confirmed bug [#10202](https://github.com/danny-avila/LibreChat/issues/10202)).

## Gotchas already paid for — don't relearn these

- **`docker-compose.yml` env lists**: `- KEY=${VAR}` — never quote the
  value (`- KEY="${VAR}"`). List-style entries don't get YAML
  quote-stripping; you'll bake literal `"` characters into the container
  and break auth silently.
- **Mongo major-version changes are not casual.** Never swap `mongo:8.0`
  for a different major version against existing data without an explicit
  supported downgrade/upgrade procedure — mismatched WiredTiger files
  cause a hard crash (`WT_PANIC`), not a graceful failure.
- **Bind-mount paths (`./mongo_data` etc.) are relative to wherever you run
  `docker compose` from.** If you ever move the project directory, the
  data doesn't follow automatically — you're pointing at a fresh empty
  path unless you move the data too.
- **containerd and Docker have separate storage configs.** Relocating
  Docker's `data-root` does NOT relocate `/var/lib/containerd` — that's a
  different service with its own config (`/etc/containerd/config.toml`).
- **`getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN mongodb`** in `api` logs almost always means
  `mongodb` itself isn't up — check `docker compose ps -a` first, not the
  network.
- **RAG embeddings run on Ollama**, not Gemini/OpenAI (cost decision).
  Ollama must be running on the **host** with `OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434`
  (default loopback-only binding is unreachable from containers) and
  `nomic-embed-text` pulled. Verify: `docker exec rag_api curl -s http://host.docker.internal:11434/api/tags`.

## Backups

```bash
/opt/aischolarhub/backup.sh        # cron'd daily at 3am — confirm it's still firing:
crontab -l
ls -la /opt/aischolarhub/backups/
```
Covers Mongo + Postgres only. `config/librechat.yaml`, `.env`, and
`docker-compose.yml` are covered by git instead (below) — `.env` itself is
gitignored, back it up separately/securely if you touch it.

## Config changes — always through git

```bash
git diff                                    # see what changed before applying
docker compose config --quiet               # validate YAML before `up`
docker compose up -d <service>               # recreate just what changed
git add docker-compose.yml config/librechat.yaml
git commit -m "what changed and why"
```

## Admin Panel notes

Separate app (`ghcr.io/clickhouse/librechat-admin-panel`), not bundled with
LibreChat itself in this custom compose setup. Needs `ADMIN_PANEL_URL` set
correctly on the `api` service to match its real public URL, or SSO breaks
([#13218](https://github.com/danny-avila/LibreChat/issues/13218)). If login
silently bounces back to `/login`: check `X-Forwarded-Proto` header is set
on the Apache vhost (session cookie won't persist without it), or fall back
to `SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=false` in its environment block.

## If something's on fire

1. `docker compose ps -a` — what's actually down, first
2. `docker compose logs <service> --tail 100` — the real reason, not a guess
3. `docker compose down && docker compose up -d` — clean recreate, safe (doesn't touch bind-mounted data)
4. Check `git log -p docker-compose.yml` — did a recent hand-edit cause this?

Symptom	Turned out to be
Instant bounce to /login	Missing X-Forwarded-Proto header (Secure cookie never set)
Delay, then 502	Cloudflare-side setting (the one you fixed by examining Cloudflare directly)
Delay, then bounce to /login again